{"state_tokens":[{"kind":"authorship","meaning":"no counted authored statement for the blob is held","token":"no authorship claim"},{"kind":"authorship","meaning":"one claimant unit of one key","token":"sole author"},{"kind":"authorship","meaning":"one derivation group of two or more keys; priority is not computed within it","token":"derived"},{"kind":"authorship","meaning":"several claimant units; one is strictly earliest at a quality this reader verified","token":"default author"},{"kind":"authorship","meaning":"several claimants (or several values of one field) and none is the default; every claimant is listed. For an edition: authorized only if approvals a key event doubts are counted, or built on an edition that is; never current, authorizes nothing. On a gate (pull, hub check, push) a label on an admitted authored whose blob is contested over the evaluated set; a label only, admission and exit are unchanged","token":"contested"},{"kind":"scope","meaning":"every status of the view is computed from the statements this reader holds; nothing is claimed about statements it never received","token":"within statements you hold"},{"kind":"scope","meaning":"every status of the view is computed from one hub's own holdings only","token":"within this hub"},{"kind":"role","meaning":"the only claimant unit","token":"author"},{"kind":"role","meaning":"the keys of the one derivation group","token":"derivers"},{"kind":"role","meaning":"a claimant after the default author; never shown as proven later","token":"later claimant"},{"kind":"role","meaning":"a claimant of a contested blob","token":"claimant"},{"kind":"field","meaning":"the field's value from the default unit, agreed by its signers","token":"default"},{"kind":"field","meaning":"no claimant declared the field; for pre-registration, not the same as exploratory","token":"undeclared"},{"kind":"field","meaning":"for a licence: none declared, or a declared value that is not an SPDX license expression (the reason is printed beside it); never read as open (C-core-67); elsewhere: nothing held establishes it. A parsed licence is shown as written with `syntax valid; identifiers not checked against the SPDX License List` and, per `LicenseRef-`, `cited (text held)`, `cited (text not held)`, `cited (location only, unverified)` or `cited (no source)`; the tool ships no licence list","token":"unknown"},{"kind":"field","meaning":"authorship is contested, so no claimant's value is the default","token":"no default (authorship contested)"},{"kind":"field","meaning":"the reader's authorship-declaration selection for the blob is not met, so no claimant's value is the default and no other declaration is substituted","token":"no default (reader's selection not met)"},{"kind":"selection","meaning":"the reader's selection names held, eligible statements, and only those are read","token":"met"},{"kind":"selection","meaning":"the pinned statement is not held; no other statement is substituted","token":"not met: statement not held"},{"kind":"selection","meaning":"the pinned statement is held but cannot serve the selection (why is printed beside it); no other statement is substituted","token":"not met: statement ineligible"},{"kind":"selection","meaning":"the followed key or identity has no eligible current claim on the content","token":"not met: no eligible current claim of the principal"},{"kind":"selection","meaning":"the followed principal has several current claims that disagree; none is preferred","token":"not met: the principal's current claims disagree"},{"kind":"selection","meaning":"the policy names an identity and this reader evaluates no identity actors; no key is followed in its place","token":"unknown (identity profile not active)"},{"kind":"selection","meaning":"a claim may act for the named identity but the statements held cannot establish it; no other claim is substituted","token":"unknown (identity eligibility not established)"},{"kind":"grade","meaning":"byte-identical re-derivation","token":"T0"},{"kind":"grade","meaning":"re-derivation matched under the named comparator, run by this reader","token":"T1"},{"kind":"grade","meaning":"task-level replication","token":"T2"},{"kind":"grade","meaning":"the blob declares no provenance, so it is a leaf, not a derivation step","token":"no derivation (no provenance)"},{"kind":"grade","meaning":"a derivation nobody else re-ran; unchecked until a second run or the reader's re-run","token":"not re-derived"},{"kind":"grade","meaning":"identical bytes under a protocol workflow: consistent with a re-run and with a copy, evidence of neither","token":"identical bytes (protocol workflow)"},{"kind":"grade","meaning":"a comparison ran to completion and the outputs disagree","token":"diverged"},{"kind":"grade","meaning":"the check could not run (no comparator, no backend, a limit); never a pass. Also a rule evaluation that could not decide, a departure check with no structured count (or none for a declared group) to compare, and a series boundary comparison with no declaration, no segments or a boundary the members' finality does not settle (a declaration later than the bound it still allows is `flagged`)","token":"unchecked"},{"kind":"grade","meaning":"the comparator could not compare the outputs. Also a departure check whose delivered sampling unit differs from the declared one (never converted), and a series boundary whose declared unit differs from the members' computed one, or whose run labels carry no order (never converted)","token":"not comparable"},{"kind":"grade","meaning":"the blob is an observation; observations carry no tier","token":"observation (not a tier)"},{"kind":"grade","meaning":"this reader holds no statement about the blob or id","token":"no statement held"},{"kind":"rule","meaning":"a rule evaluation that passed","token":"ok"},{"kind":"rule","meaning":"a rule evaluation that failed","token":"fail"},{"kind":"departure","meaning":"a departure check: the delivered sampling meets the declared n (every declared group, where groups are declared)","token":"conforms"},{"kind":"departure","meaning":"a departure check: the delivered sampling is below the declared n (the group is named); a disclosure beside the result, not a failed rule, and it never moves the grade","token":"departed"},{"kind":"series boundary","meaning":"a series boundary comparison: the declared frozen_before is no later than the boundary the members' finality rules compute; where that boundary rests on states the members asserted at capture it is shown `as captured, not re-checked` (or `as held`), never confirmed (I4)","token":"agrees"},{"kind":"series boundary","meaning":"a series boundary comparison: the declared frozen_before is later than the boundary the members' finality rules compute (or later than the bound they still allow); a disclosure beside the edition, which stays valid, and what it costs is the reader's freeze policy","token":"flagged"},{"kind":"time","meaning":"no counting anchor covers the statement","token":"none"},{"kind":"time","meaning":"an anchor this reader did not verify; self-declared, orders nothing","token":"local"},{"kind":"time","meaning":"an anchor whose proof this reader verified against block evidence it trusts","token":"bitcoin"},{"kind":"time","meaning":"the proof verified against the reader's chain view","token":"verified"},{"kind":"time","meaning":"verified against an old view at less than the settled depth; priority not computed from it","token":"verified-historical"},{"kind":"time","meaning":"only calendar attestations; a calendar's promise grants nothing. For an edition: approved by controllers of every predecessor, not yet enough for one predecessor's rule","token":"pending"},{"kind":"time","meaning":"below the reader's confirmation policy","token":"insufficient-confirmations"},{"kind":"time","meaning":"the proof blob is not held here (never fetched)","token":"missing-proof"},{"kind":"time","meaning":"the proof does not commit to the covered statement","token":"invalid-proof"},{"kind":"time","meaning":"the anchors statement itself is unusable","token":"invalid-anchor"},{"kind":"time","meaning":"the attested height is not in the reader's chain view","token":"unknown-height"},{"kind":"time","meaning":"the attested block is not on the accepted chain","token":"orphaned"},{"kind":"time","meaning":"the reader's chain view is not fresh under its policy","token":"stale-chain"},{"kind":"time","meaning":"no chain backend is configured, so no bound is verified; a state, not a failed invocation (exit 3). commons anchor headers sync --from <file> configures one","token":"backend-unconfigured"},{"kind":"time","meaning":"the configured chain backend could not be read, or its header database is not trusted (commons anchor status names why)","token":"backend-unavailable"},{"kind":"time","meaning":"a proof format, attestation, rc major, alg or critical extension this reader does not implement","token":"unsupported"},{"kind":"time","meaning":"an anchor refused under a limit of this reader; as a gate verdict, an object not admitted, with its class, reason and narrowest next step named","token":"refused"},{"kind":"statement","meaning":"signature verified and every rule this reader implements passed","token":"valid"},{"kind":"statement","meaning":"a validly signed statement of a kind the format does not list; granted nothing","token":"unknown kind"},{"kind":"statement","meaning":"a statement whose signature verified and that breaks a rule of the identity profile (rc/2): kept as evidence, counted toward nothing, never read as its key's","token":"invalid statement"},{"kind":"line","meaning":"the line reaches its log's first line through prev and merges","token":"chained"},{"kind":"line","meaning":"a predecessor is not held; shown, attributed, counted toward nothing. For an edition: every approval is on a detached line; shown, not evaluated","token":"detached"},{"kind":"statement","meaning":"chained, verified, understood and not excluded by a key event; for an identity statement, its actor eligible for the identity it names (its key's status shown beside it, not applied)","token":"counted"},{"kind":"statement","meaning":"held and shown, counted toward nothing (the reason is named)","token":"not counted"},{"kind":"actor","meaning":"the statement's signer acts for the identity it names under the grant it names, on the evidence held","token":"eligible"},{"kind":"actor","meaning":"the held evidence shows the signer does not act for that identity (the reason is named); for a grant, no act under it can count (the root retired, the grant or a cut of it is invalid)","token":"denied"},{"kind":"grant","meaning":"the grant is valid on its identity's lineage and no cut of it is held: an act under it may count (each act is still judged on its own)","token":"open"},{"kind":"grant","meaning":"the root cut the grant keeping the delegate's acts through last_good (named beside it); acts outside that history count toward nothing for the identity","token":"cut at last_good"},{"kind":"grant","meaning":"the root cut the grant keeping nothing: no act under it counts for the identity","token":"cut null"},{"kind":"bare key","meaning":"no rotate_key or revoke_key of the key is in force: its bare-key lines count by the usual rules","token":"no key event"},{"kind":"bare key","meaning":"the key's own rotate_key or revoke_key is in force: its bare-key lines after it do not count (each event's effect is named); it closes no grant naming the key","token":"self-revoked"},{"kind":"line","meaning":"an unverified line kept and not placed","token":"retained"},{"kind":"line","meaning":"two lines of one key's log from one sequence point, not yet merged; for a resource, two authorized editions with one predecessor and no merge: no edition is current","token":"FORK"},{"kind":"line","meaning":"a fork of one key's log that has cleared: a later line of the key names every other tip, so every branch is in its history; both branches stay and count","token":"merged"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"the author signed a retraction; display only, the bytes may still be served","token":"retracted"},{"kind":"bytes","meaning":"this store holds the blob's bytes and they hash correctly when read","token":"held here"},{"kind":"bytes","meaning":"this store does not hold the blob's bytes","token":"not held here"},{"kind":"fetch","meaning":"the bytes were fetched from a location and installed after the size and full-hash check; equivalent to a blob from a package","token":"fetched-and-verified"},{"kind":"fetch","meaning":"not held here and no held holds names a location for it","token":"unavailable (not held locally)"},{"kind":"fetch","meaning":"a holder said the bytes are at the location; it could not be reached (or the transfer died midway, or made no progress for --idle-timeout, default 60s), so nothing was installed","token":"unavailable (holder's word)"},{"kind":"fetch","meaning":"the location served bytes whose full hash differs; refused (intrinsic), both hashes and the location named, nothing installed","token":"unavailable (hash mismatch)"},{"kind":"fetch","meaning":"the location served a different number of bytes than the holds declares; refused (intrinsic) before the hash was relied on, nothing installed","token":"unavailable (size mismatch)"},{"kind":"fetch","meaning":"the declared size, or the stream when none is declared, exceeds the reader's fetch limit (max_fetch_bytes); refused (operational), a declared size before dialling","token":"unavailable (size limit)"},{"kind":"fetch","meaning":"the location's URI scheme is not one this reader fetches (https by default, http with --allow-http); refused before dialling","token":"unavailable (scheme not fetched)"},{"kind":"fetch","meaning":"this build has no network transport, so nothing was dialled","token":"unavailable (no transport in this build)"},{"kind":"fetch","meaning":"a dry run: the location would be dialled; nothing was","token":"would fetch (dry run)"},{"kind":"fetch","meaning":"the blob file held here does not hash to its name; never used, replaced (and quarantined) only by verified bytes","token":"stored copy corrupt"},{"kind":"verify","meaning":"a pin the statement needs is missing: a derivation input it did not pin (nothing to re-run), or a referent field an observation's class requires (no class agreement model applied)","token":"unpinned"},{"kind":"referent","meaning":"the reader's own re-check found the referent at a state that meets the declared finality rule (for an exact-bytes referent, the pinned block at that depth in this reader's synced header chain: its position re-checked, its bytes not re-read). The asserted state at capture is shown beside it, with `disagrees` set when the re-check is behind it","token":"final"},{"kind":"referent","meaning":"the observer's asserted state at capture meets the rule and no re-check of this reader confirmed it; never shown as final (I4)","token":"final (as captured, not re-checked)"},{"kind":"referent","meaning":"the state read out of the held response under the cited source profile's response layout meets the rule (the least record's state under the profile's order, so every record meets it; records that differ are disclosed beside it as \"records at R1..RF, read as R1\"; for a batch capture, the least over every logged response, \"records at R1..RF across N responses, read as R1\"); checked against the bytes, not re-checked at the source, so never shown as final (I4)","token":"final (as held)"},{"kind":"referent","meaning":"the finality rule is not met at the state shown (the state at capture, or this reader's re-check), with the state at which it would be. When a re-check computed it and the asserted state meets the rule, the two are shown beside each other with `disagrees: true`","token":"provisional"},{"kind":"referent","meaning":"a later capture of the same referent holds different bytes before finality; the observation stays true of what it pinned","token":"revised"},{"kind":"referent","meaning":"this reader's re-check found the referent replaced (a deep reorg, a dispute run; for an exact-bytes referent, the pinned block held off the accepted chain of this reader's header chain); nothing counts against the observer","token":"not canonical"},{"kind":"referent","meaning":"this reader's re-check found the pinned referent unchanged, or (exact-bytes) its block on the accepted chain of this reader's header chain (no finality rule declared)","token":"still canonical"},{"kind":"referent","meaning":"this reader's re-check of a source referent returned it (no finality rule declared)","token":"source still available"},{"kind":"referent","meaning":"this reader's re-check could not reach the source; existing corroborations stand","token":"source unavailable"},{"kind":"referent","meaning":"no finality rule declared and no re-check of this reader decided anything","token":"unknown (not re-checked by this reader)"},{"kind":"referent","meaning":"a phenomenon or method referent: its fields are pinned and it has no re-check","token":"pinned"},{"kind":"referent","meaning":"the observation's class names no referent yet","token":"no referent (class none-yet)"},{"kind":"verify","meaning":"the observation's declared finality rule cannot be evaluated by this reader","token":"finality unchecked"},{"kind":"verify","meaning":"the observation's body was kept opaque (an unsupported or critical member); nothing read from it","token":"body not interpreted"},{"kind":"verify","meaning":"the statement is not placed in its signer's log (a fork branch left out, a revoked key); it is shown, never counted","token":"counts toward nothing"},{"kind":"gate","meaning":"the object passed every check of the gate and the receiver's policy","token":"admitted"},{"kind":"gate","meaning":"admitted, with a label the reader should see (already held, detached, below trust floor, …)","token":"admitted and labelled"},{"kind":"gate","meaning":"the gate could not decide about the object (a check that could not run); never a pass","token":"could not check"},{"kind":"gate","meaning":"a control-plane path: reviewed by the maintainers, never admitted as data","token":"not applied"},{"kind":"class","meaning":"no reader could admit it (bad signature, hash mismatch, unsafe path); no override applies","token":"intrinsic"},{"kind":"class","meaning":"this reader's own policy refused it (trust floor, hub rules); a typed override naming the object may admit it","token":"reader policy"},{"kind":"class","meaning":"a limit or resource of this reader stopped it; raising the named limit is the next step","token":"operational"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"the receiver already holds this statement; nothing new is installed","token":"already held"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"the key's log is inconsistent at this line; shown, counted toward nothing","token":"incoherent"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"hub check: an added identity statement whose signer acts for the identity it names under the grant it names, judged by the evidence of the change and the base; a label only, admission and exit are unchanged","token":"actor: eligible"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"hub check: the evidence of the change and the base shows the signer does not act for that identity (the reason is named); a label only, the statement is still admitted","token":"actor: denied"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"hub check: the evidence of the change and the base cannot decide whether the signer acts for that identity (the reason is named); a label only, the statement is still admitted","token":"actor: unknown"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"hub check: an added statement signed by the root of an identity the change and the base hold, of a kind outside the closed root vocabulary (inception, grants, cuts, describes, anchors, key events); the line and the identity are named: this line stops the identity's delegates' acts from counting. A label only, the statement is still admitted; dropping it before it leaves the change restores the identity","token":"identity root: ordinary line"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"a blob no statement of the evaluated set names","token":"unreferenced"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"a statement names a blob neither the package nor the receiver holds","token":"unavailable"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"the receiver's policy does not serve the blob a statement names (not_served)","token":"not held here (policy)"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"the rc-store layout marker","token":"layout marker"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"a change to a hub's own files; not data, reviewed by the maintainers","token":"control-plane change: needs maintainer review"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"a blob the hub policy no longer serves was removed","token":"removed (not_served)"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"a blob the hub policy lists in not_served is still in the tree","token":"not served: still present"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"the receiver's re-application of the statement's intended_for, beside the signer's record: the named and the current edition's outcomes are typed `ok`, `fail` or `unchecked` members of the report row (`unchecked` when the resource or its rules could not be read), and what the publisher recorded is carried apart as its word","token":"intended_for"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"a reader-policy refusal lifted by a typed override that names this object","token":"admitted by override"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"a series boundary the freeze policy could not decide","token":"series boundary"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"the receiver's check of an edition's completeness claim (selection.refuse_incomplete): holds, or could not be checked","token":"completeness claim"},{"kind":"label","meaning":"the signer is not trusted for admission by this reader's policy; admitted and labelled (--below-floor label)","token":"below trust floor"},{"kind":"rerun","meaning":"the re-run's output equals the pinned output (bytes), or the comparator said match (protocol)","token":"match"},{"kind":"rerun","meaning":"a protocol workflow re-ran to identical bytes: consistent with a re-run and with a copy; no T0","token":"match (identical bytes)"},{"kind":"rerun","meaning":"the step exited 0 and a declared output is missing","token":"incomplete output"},{"kind":"rerun","meaning":"the step exited non-zero in an environment matching the pin (detail: the exit status)","token":"failed"},{"kind":"rerun","meaning":"a cap of this reader stopped the step (detail: the cap); could not check","token":"failed: operational"},{"kind":"rerun","meaning":"the wall-time cap stopped the step; could not check","token":"timeout"},{"kind":"rerun","meaning":"the re-run's environment differs from the pin on a field environment_match names, or the pinned environment is not available here (detail: the fields); nothing compared","token":"environment mismatch"},{"kind":"edition","meaning":"an authorized edition of the resource: every predecessor's controllers approved this body under its rule","token":"edition"},{"kind":"edition","meaning":"some predecessor's controllers did not approve this body (nobody elevates themselves)","token":"unauthorized"},{"kind":"edition","meaning":"a predecessor names nothing this reader holds as the genesis or an edition of the resource; never current","token":"orphan"},{"kind":"edition","meaning":"authorized approvals, but the body cannot be an edition (a rule no controller set meets, or a merge that does not declare differing controllers and rule)","token":"invalid"},{"kind":"readiness","meaning":"the task edition has no quorum predicate: its beneficiary's decisions settle it; nothing is counted","token":"settled by review, not by counting"},{"kind":"readiness","meaning":"the quorum is met by distinct signing keys under the edition's terms","token":"ready"},{"kind":"readiness","meaning":"the quorum is not met yet","token":"not ready"},{"kind":"submission","meaning":"a condition of the edition's terms is unchecked for the submission and none failed: left out of the lower count, in the upper one; never a veto","token":"undecided"},{"kind":"submission","meaning":"a deadline outcome: no verified bound shows the submission existed by the deadline height (a ts or a local bound meets nothing); the submission is not counted","token":"not shown"},{"kind":"decision","meaning":"the verdict of a `decide`: the beneficiary accepts the cited submissions; it settles only when the decision counts","token":"accept"},{"kind":"decision","meaning":"the verdict of a `decide`: the beneficiary rejects the cited submissions; it settles only when the decision counts","token":"reject"},{"kind":"store","meaning":"no journal record is waiting: every committed operation is installed and projected","token":"nothing pending"},{"kind":"store","meaning":"the operation reached its commit point and its statements are not all installed yet","token":"committed, pending install"},{"kind":"store","meaning":"the operation is committed and not finished: a blob it names is missing, or its projections are untrusted; status and fsck name the cause, and `repair` finishes it once the cause is fixed","token":"committed, needs repair"},{"kind":"recovery","meaning":"a pending operation was finished (on open, or by repair)","token":"replayed"},{"kind":"recovery","meaning":"a done operation's projections were rebuilt (on open, or by repair)","token":"projected"},{"kind":"recovery","meaning":"a committed operation could not be finished on open or by repair: a blob it names is missing, or a projection failed; `repair` finishes it once the cause is fixed","token":"needs repair"},{"kind":"recovery","meaning":"a committed operation could not be finished on open (the error is printed); its statements are hidden and its signers' writes refused until `repair` or a later open finishes it","token":"replay failed"},{"kind":"recovery","meaning":"repair was named an operation id no journal record has: the operation is finished, or was never committed here","token":"nothing to repair"},{"kind":"recovery","meaning":"a journal record failed to decode or verify and was moved aside; nothing from it installed","token":"quarantined"},{"kind":"recovery","meaning":"a corrupt stored copy was quarantined and the verified line installed","token":"replaced statement"},{"kind":"recovery","meaning":"a stale temporary file was removed","token":"removed temporary"},{"kind":"recovery","meaning":"a gc run stopped after moving a blob aside and before deciding; the verified file was put back","token":"restored blob"},{"kind":"history","meaning":"this store appends a line to its local operation history when an operation finishes (bounded, best-effort, never transported, not authoritative)","token":"history on"},{"kind":"history","meaning":"this store keeps no operation history; `history` lists nothing","token":"history off"},{"kind":"history","meaning":"a history entry: the operation's statements were installed and its journal record moved to done, at the local time shown (this machine's clock)","token":"finished"},{"kind":"since","meaning":"something explain prints beyond its causes (a token, a count, a view) differs from the saved explain","token":"answer changed"},{"kind":"since","meaning":"everything explain prints beyond its causes is as in the saved explain","token":"answer unchanged"},{"kind":"since","meaning":"a statement is an input of the answer now and was not in the saved explain (its id)","token":"statement added"},{"kind":"since","meaning":"a statement of the saved explain is no longer an input of the answer (its id)","token":"statement removed"},{"kind":"since","meaning":"a rotate_key or revoke_key of an input's signer arrived (its id and kind): it decides which of that key's lines count","token":"key event"},{"kind":"since","meaning":"an input's statement status differs (its id, before and after)","token":"status changed"},{"kind":"since","meaning":"an input's place in its signer's log differs, e.g. detached to chained (its id, before and after)","token":"line changed"},{"kind":"since","meaning":"whether an input counts differs (its id, before and after); a key event or a missing predecessor is the usual cause","token":"counted changed"},{"kind":"since","meaning":"the hub policy digest differs (before and after)","token":"policy changed"},{"kind":"since","meaning":"the reader policy digest differs; each entry one side has and the other lacks is named","token":"reader policy changed"},{"kind":"since","meaning":"the time policy fingerprint differs","token":"time policy changed"},{"kind":"since","meaning":"the tool version, commit or time verifier differs","token":"evaluator changed"},{"kind":"since","meaning":"the time context of the answer differs (a read time it depends on, or the clock no longer read)","token":"time context changed"}]}
